<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    nexus-cefa1.4 — schema type-hygiene pass, Tier B, P3 (epic nexus-cefa1;
    plan of record T2 nexus/plan-schema-type-hygiene-2026-08-12 [22360]).
    Template: telemetry-004-type-hygiene.xml (nexus-cefa1.3, P2) — the
    closest sibling (same one-ALTER-per-table shape, same jsonbOrNull /
    JSONB.data() wire-preservation pattern, same rollback style).

    Retires four RDR-152 SQLite-port columns across TWO tables, in TWO
    changesets (one per table — document_aspects and aspect_promotion_log
    are different tables, so this mirrors telemetry-004's "one ALTER per
    table" shape rather than folding both tables into a single ALTER):

    Changeset 1 — nexus.document_aspects (Tier B, TEXT -> jsonb):
    - extras (nullable, no default per aspects-001-baseline.xml:66) -> jsonb
      NULL, via TYPE jsonb USING NULLIF(extras, '')::jsonb.
    - salient_sentences (nullable, no default per aspects-001-
      baseline.xml:72) -> jsonb NULL, via the identical USING clause.
      Neither column carries a DEFAULT or NOT NULL to DROP/restore — unlike
      telemetry-004's is_batch (NOT NULL DEFAULT 0) or catalog-031's
      legacy_grandfathered, this changeset is a bare TYPE ... USING with no
      DROP DEFAULT / SET DEFAULT bracketing, because there is nothing to
      drop or re-set.

    Changeset 2 — nexus.aspect_promotion_log (Tier A, INTEGER -> boolean):
    - column_added: INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 -> boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT
      false, via DROP DEFAULT -> TYPE boolean USING (column_added <> 0) ->
      SET DEFAULT false. Same shape as telemetry-004's is_batch / catalog-
      031-3's legacy_grandfathered.
    - pruned: INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 -> boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
      identical shape.
    - rows_pruned stays INTEGER, untouched — it is a COUNT (rows affected
      by a prune), not a duplicate of the pruned FLAG; conflating the two
      was considered and rejected at plan time (T2 nexus/plan-schema-type-
      hygiene-2026-08-12: "aspect_promotion_log.rows_pruned vs .pruned —
      NOT duplicates: count vs flag ... Both stay; pruned -> boolean.").
    NOT NULL is preserved automatically across ALTER COLUMN TYPE on both
    columns (never touched); only DEFAULT is dropped and re-set because a
    numeric DEFAULT 0 is not valid input for a boolean column.

    ALTER COLUMN TYPE is ordinary DDL (an ACCESS EXCLUSIVE table rewrite),
    not RLS-filtered DML — no FORCE RLS toggle needed for either changeset,
    and neither touches a row via INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE.

    Data-safety evidence:
    - document_aspects.extras / .salient_sentences: T2 nexus/schema-hygiene-
      p0-preflight-2026-08-15 [22588] (nexus-cefa1.1), cloud (the only
      populated deployment; this box's local substrate is a fresh hermetic
      pytest engine with no seeded data): total_rows=1030 for BOTH columns,
      null_count=0, empty_string_count=0, invalid_cast_count=0 for BOTH —
      every row already holds valid, non-empty JSON. The NULLIF(...,'')
      ::jsonb USING clause above therefore has nothing to convert on either
      column and is confirmed safe.
    - aspect_promotion_log.column_added / .pruned: NOT part of the P0 probe
      (Tier A boolean columns, not Tier B jsonb — the P0 probe audits Tier
      B jsonb-target columns plus the four Tier-A timestamp columns; this
      table's two INTEGER flag columns were never in either probe's scope).
      Their live value domain was instead verified by reading BOTH writers:
      - Java: AspectRepository.recordPromotion / .importPromotionRow /
        .importPromotionBatch each derive column_added and pruned as
        `Boolean.TRUE.equals(body.get(...)) ? 1 : 0` before every INSERT —
        the column's value domain is mechanically {0, 1}, never any other
        integer.
      - Python: aspect_promotion.py's own changeset-template docstring (the
        canonical "how to promote a field" recipe every real promotion
        follows, since the runtime promotion verb itself is retired per
        nexus-70x7y) writes literal `1` / `0` for column_added / pruned in
        its INSERT ... SELECT sample.
      `USING (column_added <> 0)` / `USING (pruned <> 0)` are therefore
      exhaustive and safe by construction, independent of any live-data
      probe — same reasoning telemetry-004 applied to hook_failures.is_batch.

    Consumer audit (nexus-cefa1.4, mirroring nexus-cefa1.2/.3's sweeps):
    - extras / salient_sentences: the wire is ALREADY a JSON string/dict/
      list end to end. AspectHandler.serializeAspectBody already
      JSON-serializes List/Map values for both fields before they reach the
      repository (Python clients send dicts/lists; Jackson deserializes
      them as ArrayList/LinkedHashMap); a caller-supplied pre-serialized
      String passes through unchanged. This changeset does not change that
      wire shape, only the storage column's own type — AspectRepository's
      write sites wrap the incoming JSON string in JSONB.valueOf via the
      shared JsonbSupport.jsonbOrNull helper (extracted from
      TelemetryRepository, nexus-cefa1.3, rather than copy-pasted a second
      time), and read sites (recordToMap, getSalientSentences) unwrap via
      JSONB.data() so the wire stays exactly the JSON text it always was.
      AspectRepository's operator-fast-path SQL
      (filterBySourceUris/groupByField's `COALESCE(extras,'{}')::json#>>
      '{key}'` expression, RDR-089 bead nexus-l9hd8) is UNCHANGED and
      verified to keep working: COALESCE coerces the untyped '{}' literal
      to jsonb to match the (now-native) jsonb `extras` column, `::json`
      remains a legal jsonb->json cast, and `#>>` operates on json exactly
      as before — this is a raw SQL string built by fieldExpression(), not
      tied to jOOQ's generated column type, so it is unaffected by the
      column's underlying storage type either way.
    - column_added / pruned: the wire is ALSO already boolean end to end —
      AspectRepositoryTest's existing recordPromotion/listPromotions round-
      trip tests already write/read Java Booleans on the body Map (`body.
      put("column_added", true)`, asserted via `Boolean.TRUE.equals(...)`),
      and Python's enrich.py CLI reader (`e["pruned"]` used in a truthy
      `if`) is compatible with either a JSON int or a JSON boolean. This
      changeset retires the `? 1 : 0` / `!= 0` integer shims in
      AspectRepository.recordPromotion / .listPromotions /
      .importPromotionRow / .importPromotionBatch — the wire shape itself
      does not change.
    - StagingPromoteOps.finalizeTenant's document_aspects promote (Class-D,
      anti-join on (collection, source_path)) selects staged `extras` into
      the now-jsonb DOCUMENT_ASPECTS.EXTRAS column — the staged column
      itself stays TEXT (staging is deliberately typeless), so the promote
      SELECT needs an explicit cast. See StagingPromoteOps.parseStagedJson
      (new, sibling of parseStagedTimestamp/parseStagedTimestampNullable)
      and its call site. salient_sentences is NOT part of that INSERT's
      column list (verified: the promote's document_aspects column list
      omits it), so no staging-side change is needed for that column.
    - No text-equality or hash consumer of extras/salient_sentences was
      found (plan-of-record fact 6 audit): grepped src/nexus and
      service/src/main for aspect dedup / match_text derivation touching
      these two fields — none exists. AspectRepository's own conflict key
      is (tenant_id, collection, source_path), never extras' content.

    ANALYZE after each rewrite (BUG-0148 invariant, rdr180-16-analyze-
    rewritten-tables precedent, mechanically enforced by
    tests/test_changelog_analyze_lint.py) — each ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE
    above resets its table's planner statistics.

    Rollback: document_aspects mirrors telemetry-004's batch_doc_ids
    rollback exactly (nullable, no-default TEXT columns pre-migration —
    TYPE TEXT USING col::text casts a jsonb NULL back to a TEXT NULL for
    free, no COALESCE-to-'' needed). aspect_promotion_log mirrors
    telemetry-004's is_batch / catalog-031-3's legacy_grandfathered exactly
    (TYPE INTEGER USING (CASE WHEN col THEN 1 ELSE 0 END), DEFAULT 0
    restored) for both column_added and pruned.

    Ordering: registered after telemetry-004-type-hygiene.xml (P2) and
    before the grants-nexus-svc.xml runAlways block, NOT back in the
    aspects-00N family's own section near the top of the changelog. This
    matches the master changelog's established convention for every new
    changeset since RDR-156 (catalog-031, telemetry-004, etc. all append
    near the current tail rather than splicing back into their family's
    original block) — see db.changelog-master.xml's own header on the
    telemetry-004 <include> for the identical reasoning applied there.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <!-- ── Changeset aspects-003-1-document-aspects-type-hygiene ──────────────── -->
    <changeSet id="aspects-003-1-document-aspects-type-hygiene" author="nexus-cefa1.4">
        <comment>
            document_aspects.extras TEXT -> jsonb NULL; document_aspects.salient_sentences
            TEXT -> jsonb NULL (ONE ALTER TABLE, one rewrite).
        </comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.document_aspects
    ALTER COLUMN extras TYPE jsonb USING NULLIF(extras, '')::jsonb,
    ALTER COLUMN salient_sentences TYPE jsonb USING NULLIF(salient_sentences, '')::jsonb;

-- BUG-0148 invariant (rdr180-16-analyze-rewritten-tables precedent, mechanically
-- enforced by tests/test_changelog_analyze_lint.py): the ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE
-- above rewrites document_aspects and resets its planner statistics.
ANALYZE nexus.document_aspects;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true">
ALTER TABLE nexus.document_aspects
    ALTER COLUMN extras TYPE TEXT USING extras::text,
    ALTER COLUMN salient_sentences TYPE TEXT USING salient_sentences::text;

ANALYZE nexus.document_aspects;
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- ── Changeset aspects-003-2-promotion-log-type-hygiene ─────────────────── -->
    <changeSet id="aspects-003-2-promotion-log-type-hygiene" author="nexus-cefa1.4">
        <comment>
            aspect_promotion_log.column_added INTEGER -> boolean; aspect_promotion_log.pruned
            INTEGER -> boolean (ONE ALTER TABLE, one rewrite). rows_pruned (a COUNT) is
            untouched -- not a duplicate of the pruned flag.
        </comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.aspect_promotion_log
    ALTER COLUMN column_added DROP DEFAULT,
    ALTER COLUMN column_added TYPE boolean USING (column_added &lt;&gt; 0),
    ALTER COLUMN column_added SET DEFAULT false,
    ALTER COLUMN pruned DROP DEFAULT,
    ALTER COLUMN pruned TYPE boolean USING (pruned &lt;&gt; 0),
    ALTER COLUMN pruned SET DEFAULT false;

-- BUG-0148 invariant: the ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE above rewrites
-- aspect_promotion_log and resets its planner statistics.
ANALYZE nexus.aspect_promotion_log;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true">
ALTER TABLE nexus.aspect_promotion_log
    ALTER COLUMN column_added DROP DEFAULT,
    ALTER COLUMN column_added TYPE INTEGER USING (CASE WHEN column_added THEN 1 ELSE 0 END),
    ALTER COLUMN column_added SET DEFAULT 0,
    ALTER COLUMN pruned DROP DEFAULT,
    ALTER COLUMN pruned TYPE INTEGER USING (CASE WHEN pruned THEN 1 ELSE 0 END),
    ALTER COLUMN pruned SET DEFAULT 0;

ANALYZE nexus.aspect_promotion_log;
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
